<title>BELGIUM: EU dismisses Boeing-related trade war comment.</title>
<headline>EU dismisses Boeing-related trade war comment.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Competition Commissioner Karel Van Miert dismissed press comments on Wednesday that the merger between Boeing and McDonnell Douglas could trigger a transatlantic trade war as &quot;totally nonsensical&quot;.</p>
<p>Van Miert's spokesman quoted him as saying that there was no reason for rumours or comments that the deal would result in a trade war between the European Union and the United States and it was wrong to envisage catastrophe scenarios at this stage.</p>
<p>&quot;Catastrophe or worst-case scenarios, we are not there,&quot; the spokesman, Willy Helin, said adding that there were still more than two months of discussions and contacts ahead. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
